 # OpenVDB (VDB)
 
-Also called: OpenVDB Hierarchical Compression, VDB
+Also called: OpenVDB Format, OpenVDB Hierarchical Compression, VDB
 
 ## Overview
-OpenVDB is a sparse voxel representation used for the hierarchical encoding and compression of volumetric grids, featuring fast $O(1)$ random access for both modification and retrieval operations [S1]. It solves the problem of efficiently storing and accessing vast volumetric datasets where large regions are empty, by storing voxels sparsely so that empty space costs almost nothing on disk or in memory [S2]. Unlike dense texture-based approaches, OpenVDB uses a shallow, four-level tree structure with direct-access bitmasks to enable efficient traversal and modification, making it the de facto standard file format for storing volumetric data in production rendering and visual effects [S1, S2].
+OpenVDB is a sparse voxel representation used for the hierarchical encoding and compression of volumetric grids, featuring fast $O(1)$ random access for modification and retrieval operations [S1]. It solves the problem of efficiently storing and accessing vast volumetric datasets where large regions are empty, by storing voxels sparsely so that empty space costs almost nothing on disk or in memory [S2, unofficial]. Unlike dense texture-based approaches, OpenVDB uses a shallow, four-level tree structure with direct-access bitmasks to enable efficient traversal and modification, making it the de facto standard file format for storing volumetric data in production rendering and visual effects [S1][S2, unofficial].
 
