-### OpenVDB Data Structure
-The volume object is aimed at smoke simulation, procedural volume generation with modifiers, and importing OpenVDB files from other applications [S4]. The object is of type `OB_VOLUME` and uses a Volume datablock as object data [S4]. The Volume datablock contains a list of volume grids, which may come from a file or be procedurally generated by a modifier [S4]. Each VolumeGrid contains one OpenVDB grid [S4]. An OpenVDB grid consists of Metadata (name and other fields), a Transform (linear or perspective transform from voxel index to object space), and a Tree (a tree data structure of nodes, with leaf nodes that contain a grid of $8 \times 8 \times 8$ voxels) [S4].
+#### OpenVDB Data Structure
+The volume object is aimed at smoke simulation, procedural volume generation with modifiers, and importing OpenVDB files from other applications [S5]. The object is of type `OB_VOLUME` and uses a Volume datablock as object data [S5]. The Volume datablock contains a list of volume grids, which may come from a file or be procedurally generated by a modifier [S5]. Each VolumeGrid contains one OpenVDB grid [S5]. An OpenVDB grid consists of Metadata (name and other fields), a Transform (linear or perspective transform from voxel index to object space), and a Tree (a tree data structure of nodes, with leaf nodes that contain a grid of $8 \times 8 \times 8$ voxels) [S5].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
 *   **Time Complexity:** Fast $O(1)$ random access for modification and retrieval operations [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Sparse storage means memory usage is proportional to the number of active voxels and nodes, not the total domain volume [S2]. However, broad tile initialization can lead to significant overhead if data points are far from allocated sections [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Sparse storage means memory usage is proportional to the number of active voxels and nodes, not the total domain volume [S2, unofficial]. Broad tile initialization can lead to significant overhead if data points are far from allocated sections [S4, unofficial].
 *   **Performance:** Well-suited for visual effects rendering of volumetric data from fluid simulation [S1].
-*   **Strengths:** Efficient compression of sparse data, fast random access, integration with production renderers (Cycles) and VFX software (Houdini, Cinema 4D) [S1, S2].
-*   **Limitations:** Memory overhead from tile initialization; trade-off between leaf size and insertion time; custom datatypes increase memory usage [S1][S3, unofficial].
-*   **When to Use:** When rendering large, sparse volumetric datasets (e.g., smoke, fire) where empty space is significant, and fast random access is required [S1, S2].
-*   **When Not to Use:** When data is dense and sparse storage overhead outweighs benefits, or when dynamic modification with complex custom datatypes is frequent and memory is constrained [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Strengths:** Efficient compression of sparse data, fast random access, integration with production renderers (Cycles) and VFX software (Houdini, Cinema 4D) [S1][S2, unofficial].
+*   **Limitations:** Memory overhead from tile initialization; trade-off between leaf size and insertion time; custom datatypes increase memory usage [S1][S4, unofficial].
