 ## Background
-OpenVDB was originally developed at DreamWorks Animation, open sourced in 2012, honored with an Academy Award for technical achievement, and is now maintained under the Academy Software Foundation [S2]. It is the de facto standard file format for storing volumetric data, analogous to how EXR is the standard for HDR images [S2]. It is widely used in production rendering and visual effects software such as Houdini, Cinema 4D, and Redshift [S1, S2].
